Linus,

The following changes since commit e9e7183fd2677aca24e90ca1556d4afe7436d42d:

  Merge branch 'fix/asoc' into for-linus (2012-05-05 11:27:26 +0200)

are available in the git repository at:


  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tiwai/sound.git tags/sound-3.4

for you to fetch changes up to 9ea3356d7979909d19252f7e552fb879643eaa70:

  Merge tag 'asoc-3.4' of git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/broonie/sound into for-linus (2012-05-09 14:03:29 +0200)

----------------------------------------------------------------

sound fixes for 3.4-rc7

Slightly more than expected as rc7, but all are reasonablly small fixes.
A few additions of HD-audio fixup entries, a couple of other regression
fixes including a revert, and a few other trivial oneliners.

----------------------------------------------------------------
Andre Schramm (1):
      ALSA: hdsp - Provide ioctl_compat

David Henningsson (1):
      ALSA: HDA: Lessen CPU usage when waiting for chip to respond

Guennadi Liakhovetski (1):
      ASoC: sh: fix migor.c compilation

Mark Hills (1):
      ALSA: echoaudio: Remove incorrect part of assertion

Takashi Iwai (5):
      ALSA: hda/realtek - Add a fixup for Acer Aspire 5739G
      ALSA: hda/realtek - Add missing CD-input pin for MSI-7350 mobo
      ALSA: hda/realtek - Call alc_auto_parse_customize_define() always after fixup
      Revert "ALSA: hda - Set codec to D3 forcibly even if not used"
      Merge tag 'asoc-3.4' of git://git.kernel.org/.../broonie/sound into for-linus

